WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:02.700
Cutover proves the new
estate can be built.

2
00:00:02.700 --> 00:00:06.388
The first locked-out user on Monday
proves whether it can be run.

3
00:00:06.388 --> 00:00:10.263
A user changed phones; a new
hire needs an account by nine.

4
00:00:10.263 --> 00:00:12.037
Each lands at the help desk.

5
00:00:12.037 --> 00:00:15.811
If the new model can't handle it
safely, the desk finds a way:

6
00:00:15.811 --> 00:00:19.024
an emergency admin account
that never goes away,

7
00:00:19.024 --> 00:00:24.324
an email treated as the request, a temporary
password sent back to the same inbox.

8
00:00:24.324 --> 00:00:26.763
Each shortcut is reasonable on the day.

9
00:00:26.763 --> 00:00:29.737
Together they rebuild the
estate you just replaced.

10
00:00:29.737 --> 00:00:34.437
The decision for the CIO: call a
wave complete only after a reset,

11
00:00:34.437 --> 00:00:38.775
an unlock, a joiner and a leaver
have run under the new model.

12
00:00:38.775 --> 00:00:40.940
Next, the riskiest of those.
